       </draw:frame>Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure0" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">1</text:sequence>: Block diagram for an async buck converter</text:p>
     </draw:text-box>
    </draw:frame></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P6"><text:span text:style-name="T1">This converter is designed to step down a 10V input to a 5V output, while maintaining 1A current delivery to the load. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T2">The inductor current should have a peak to peak ripple which is within 20%-40% of its DC value, and the output voltage should have a peak to peak ripple which is at most 1% of its DC value. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7">Following TI SLVA477B, we can calculate what our inductance and capacitance should be in this circuit, matching what is available in the lab.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P3" text:outline-level="1">Simulation</text:h>
   <text:h text:style-name="P8" text:outline-level="2">Simulation Performance</text:h>
   <text:h text:style-name="P9" text:outline-level="1">Physical Prototype</text:h>
   <text:h text:style-name="P8" text:outline-level="2">Part Selection</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P10">Include a table of measured components</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P8" text:outline-level="2"><text:soft-page-break/>Prototype Performance</text:h>
   <text:h text:style-name="P3" text:outline-level="1">Appendix I – LTSpice models</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P11">Below are the models which I sourced from the Internet. For each model, copy and paste the contents of each file to their own file, in the same location as your project, and create an include directive to import the file to your project. Then, hold control and click on the device, and update the `<text:span text:style-name="T3">Value</text:span>` field to reflect the correct device (e.g., for a PMOS, change `<text:span text:style-name="T3">Value</text:span>` to `<text:span text:style-name="T3">irf9530</text:span>`; for the Diode, change `<text:span text:style-name="T3">Value</text:span>` to `<text:span text:style-name="T3">1N4004</text:span>`).</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P12" text:outline-level="2" text:is-list-header="true"><text:span text:style-name="T4">IRF9530 PMOS</text:span></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Preformatted_20_Text">.SUBCKT irf9530 1 2 3</text:p>
